  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seychelles Second Sustainable and Inclusive Growth Development Policy Operation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Program Development Objectives are to support the Government of Seychelles to: (i) strengthen financial stability and the business environment; (ii) promote fiscal transparency; and (iii) enhance environmental and social resilience</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Second Sustainable and Inclusive Growth Development Policy Operation for Seychelles supports the government across three interconnected pillars: strengthening financial stability and the business environment, promoting fiscal transparency, and enhancing environmental and social resilience. These pillars are closely aligned with the Seychelles National Development Strategy 2024-2028, which charts a course toward diversified, inclusive, and climate-resilient development across six areas including economic transformation, public service modernization, health, education, law and order, and environmental sustainability. The DPO&apos;s first pillar advances legislative reforms in non-bank credit regulation, cybercrime, and renewable energy; its second pillar targets revenue transparency through transfer pricing rules and improved budget efficiency; and its third pillar addresses waste management and youth risk behavior. Together, these measures form a coherent reform agenda that reinforces the country&apos;s long-term development priorities.</narrative>
  </description>
